  "slug": "clifford-sampling-345a",
  "summary": "Three new simulators handle non-Clifford, coherent and general Kraus noise in QEC-style circuits while remaining exact or reaching distance-9 surface codes.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is classical machinery for sampling noisy quantum circuits, with error-correction workloads as the main target. MASQ is an exact measurement-adaptive sampler for near-Clifford QEC circuits that materializes only the non-Clifford contributions relevant to measurements. Compiled Clifford-augmented matrix product states accelerate coherent-noise QEC simulation and reach distance-9 surface codes. Pre-trajectory sampling with batched GPU execution is extended to mid-circuit measurements and general Kraus channels while remaining exact. A second strand treats quantum hardware or circuits as samplers. One study quantifies how physical qubit embeddings affect annealer sampling of the 2D Ising model and feeds QPU-learned proposals into corrected Monte Carlo. Another trains a hypernetwork that maps Hamiltonian parameters to circuit angles for ground-state samplers. A third finds the Fisher trace uninformative for certifying Born machines and shows that kernel verdicts depend on tolerance. Peripheral items cover stopping thresholds for noisy Grover search under Drude-Lorentz noise, commutator-guided repair of shallow circuits, and Koopman-von Neumann flow simulation with surface-code resource estimates.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-22"
}
